    "blurb": "The show shines on a blistering Playing In The Band that launches a fiery Deal, an inspired Brokedown Palace, and a soaring Dark Star. Jerry’s wailing guitar and Phil’s booming bass drive the high‑energy flow, while the rhythm section stays tight throughout. Soundboard sources capture the performance clearly despite minor hiss.",
    "review": "October 26, 1972 at Cincinnati Music Hall finds the Dead in top form, especially on that second set where everything clicks. The night erupts with a thunderous Playing In The Band that propels into a scorching Deal and then into an expansive Dark Star, showcasing Jerry’s wailing “wawa” tone and Phil’s powerful bass lines. Brokedown Palace follows, its gentle lyricism lifted by Jerry’s soaring solos and Keith’s tasteful piano textures. The band rides this momentum into Sugar Magnolia and a heartfelt Sing Me Back Home before closing with One More Saturday Night, keeping the energy high from start to finish. While the recordings carry a touch of hiss and occasional mix quirks—Mickey’s bass drum can be overly forward and Phil is sometimes buried—the overall clarity of the Miller soundboards lets the nuances shine, making this a must‑listen performance from the early ‘70s.",
